event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_065bf45199317461016acd1f8087188197a365c9223aec4c28","output_index":0,"sequence_number":80,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering Python transformations**\n\nI'm thinking about how to use Python for transformations via bash. I guess I need to focus on making edits in bulk, which might require me to programmatically handle replacements. Using an exact method could be the way to go if I'm dealing with large datasets. It's all about efficiently managing these edits! I wonder what the best approach will be for ensuring accuracy while transforming the data effectively."}

